-- Diplomatic Appointments (Selection Process) Bill 2026 (Cth), first reading print (Senate),
-- 7 September 2026 (file 26S2721).
-- LQA step 8A (Demonstrate), 2 October 2026: assertions written as evidence for findings in
-- incidents.json. Not part of the encoding certified at 6H and not listed in coverage.json;
-- it imports the certified modules (through cases.l4, for its builders and people) and
-- changes nothing in them.

IMPORT `cases`

§ `L-04: a Committee that never decides is never dissolved, and blocks any other`

-- The Japan Committee is established on 11 January 2028 and given its list on 18 January. It
-- never meets. Two years later it is still in existence (s 10(5) dissolves it only on its notice),
-- and s 12(8) still bars a second Committee for the appointment.
`a Committee that never meets` MEANS `an undecided Committee established on` (`the day` 2028 1 11) `, list given on` (`the day` 2028 1 18) `with the list` `the Japan list`

#ASSERT `the Committee` `a Committee that never meets` `is in existence on` (`the day` 2030 1 18)
#ASSERT NOT `section 12(8) allows a Committee to be established on` (`the day` 2030 1 18) `beside` (LIST `a Committee that never meets`)
#ASSERT `the last day for the Committee's notice for` `a Committee that never meets` `in` `the world` EQUALS `the day` 2028 3 20

-- With one member absent the meeting is inquorate (s 13(2)), so even a referral back is no
-- decision under s 10(3) (s 13(1)): a Committee short of a member cannot reach s 9(3)(b).
`a two-member Committee` MEANS `a Committee established on` (`the day` 2028 1 11) `, given on` (`the day` 2028 1 18) `the list` `the Japan list` `, meeting with` 2 `present voting` 0 `to` 2 `, giving on` (`the day` 2028 3 1) `notice` `referring the matter back to the Minister`

#ASSERT NOT `the Committee referred the matter back` `a two-member Committee`

§ `L-07: the s 10(2)(b) cap applies to a list of 2 or 3 under s 10(6)`

-- The second India Committee (after a referral) is given 3 candidates, 2 of them with a
-- significant political affiliation. Section 10(6) permits the size; s 10(2)(b) (2 to 4
-- candidates: only 1 affiliated) still applies, and is breached.
`India second Committee with two affiliated` MEANS `an undecided Committee established on` (`the day` 2028 3 1) `, list given on` (`the day` 2028 3 3) `with the list` (LIST `listed without reasons` `Alex`, `listed with reasons` `Gray`, `listed with reasons` `Kai`)

#ASSERT `the Committee` `India second Committee with two affiliated` `is a second or subsequent Committee after` `India Committees`
#ASSERT `the list for` `India second Committee with two affiliated` `after` `India Committees` `has a permitted number of candidates`
#ASSERT NOT `s 10(2)(b) and (c) are met by the list for` `India second Committee with two affiliated`

§ `T-19: s 15 turns on the day the term starts`

-- The same appointment of a sitting member, made on the same day in the first year, is inside or
-- outside the Act according to the term start the appointing instrument chooses.
`Drew, term from 1 March 2028` MEANS `the appointment of` `Drew` `to` `Ambassador to Ireland` `made on` (`the day` 2027 9 1) `, term from` (`the day` 2028 3 1) `, after an appointment on` (`the day` 2024 1 10) `, with Committees` EMPTY
`Drew, term from 2 March 2028` MEANS `the appointment of` `Drew` `to` `Ambassador to Ireland` `made on` (`the day` 2027 9 1) `, term from` (`the day` 2028 3 2) `, after an appointment on` (`the day` 2024 1 10) `, with Committees` EMPTY

#ASSERT `the appointment` `Drew, term from 1 March 2028` `was made in accordance with this Act, in` `the world`
#ASSERT NOT `the appointment` `Drew, term from 2 March 2028` `was made in accordance with this Act, in` `the world`
